{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112450","id":2982070774,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6xvsn2","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112450","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112450.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112450.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112450","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112450/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112450/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112450/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/2f029bc7bf07c4f3c1eb6604244b79a3f4179068","number":112450,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix NodeOneShot doesn't reset correctly","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- Fix partially https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111938\r\n\r\nWhen a reset is triggered during a OneShot run, the shot port's animation should reset, but it was not doing so.\r\n\r\nThis PR change ensures that when a reset is triggered during a OneShot run, the shot port's animation will reset.\r\n\r\nIf a reset is triggered during a fade-out, the in port's animation will reset and play again after the abort.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/873a62b5-1302-4090-9b50-5dc7e8ed9f9f\r\n\r\nBTW, abort is performed when reset is triggered during fadeout is the same as before. As I explained somewhere earlier, this is because the internal state is already in the next state (running \"in\" port's animation) when fadeout starts.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis issue has existed since the beginning of 4.0. I consider this a bug, but since it involves a bit of behavior change, I added a break compat label.\r\n\r\nTo preserve the previous behavior where it wouldn't reset during reset, you must explicitly avoid triggering reset. AnimationNodes that could trigger a reset should have this setting, so you can disable it.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"577\" height=\"338\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f88f7cd6-010f-45f9-a845-39a96f37fc35\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"572\" height=\"194\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/94b72bd7-56e8-4092-a73b-7bd2c99d881b\" />\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":955079684,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw5NTUwNzk2ODQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/breaks%20compat","name":"breaks compat","description":"","color":"b64245","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666705648,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA1NjQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:animation","name":"